.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-DELETE-OBJECT-ATTRIBUTE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-delete-object-attribute \- remove an attribute from a storage object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm delete-object-attribute
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes one user-defined attribute from a storage object. The object
itself and its bytes are untouched; only the named attribute is
dropped.
.PP
The attribute must exist: deleting one that was never stored is
reported as an error rather than silently succeeding, for the same
reason adding and setting are strict about the name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the object. Required.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the attribute to remove. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The attribute was removed. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no object
with that ERN exists, the object belongs to another account, or the
object has no attribute of that name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm delete-object-attribute \e
    --ern ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:object:mix/PIM-4269.xml \e
    --name revision
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-add-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-object-attribute (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-list-object-attributes (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-object (1)
